          m_Value0: 14442780617360086518
          m_Value1: 17299616833270263656
        Parents: []
        PortModels: []
        Text: "NOTE: IsInGrappleWindow Abort should be BOTH: \nif it changes moment-to-moment
          and should immediately change behavior"
    - rid: 7112529932246582179
      type: {class: StickyNoteModel, ns: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework, asm: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework}
      data:
        Position: {x: -621.44653, y: -55.608433}
        ID:
          m_Value0: 8938443015604117378
          m_Value1: 18101329846442009593
        Parents: []
        PortModels: []
        Text: "NOTE: Defense checks (optional prototype)\n- PlayerInFront / PlayerBehind
          \u2192 None or Self (Abort mode)\n- Don\u2019t use Both (Abort mode) unless
          you want constant interrupting. This can cause jittery 'flip-flop' behaviour
          if the player moves around the edge of the front arc.\n\n- Shield potential
          mistake: If you put 'RaiseShield' as a long-running action, don\u2019t
          make it constantly abort itself due to a twitchy directional condition.
          \n- Keep those directional conditions non-aborting or smoothed."
    - rid: 7112529932407013731
