    - rid: 7112529932407014053
      type: {class: StickyNoteModel, ns: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework, asm: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework}
      data:
        Position: {x: 821.2726, y: -256.2211}
        ID:
          m_Value0: 3907220000712703820
          m_Value1: 14611585125787537659
        Parents: []
        PortModels: []
        Text: "WHAT EACH ABORT MODE DOES (SUMMARY)\n\n- NONE -\nCondition only checked
          once on entry\n\u274C Almost never correct for combat AI.\n\n- SELF -\nRe-evaluates
          while its own branch is running.\nGood for:\n\"Stay stunned while stunned\"\n\"Stop
          attack if condition becomes false\"\n\n- LOWER PRIORITY -\nIf this condition
          becomes true, it aborts branches below it.\nGood for:\nInterrupting Chase
          when Attack becomes valid\n\n- BOTH - \nSelf + Lower Priority.\n\u2705
          BEST DEFAULT for COMBAT LOGIC. "
    - rid: 7112529932488278581
      type: {class: StickyNoteModel, ns: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework, asm: Unity.Behavior.GraphFramework}
      data:
        Position: {x: 802.944, y: -840.92334}
        ID:
          m_Value0: 15917420568275680195
          m_Value1: 17709539309018509115
        Parents: []
        PortModels: []
        Text: 'CHEAT SHEET FOR ABORT MODE CHOICE


          - Set to BOTH -


          IsDead


          IsStunned


          IsKnockedDown


          HasTarget
          (only if losing target should instantly exit combat)


          - Set
          to LOWER PRIORITY -


          InRange + CanAttack (punch/swing/slam/fire)


          PlayerTooClose
          / TooFar (movement choices)


          GrappleWindowOpen (if it should
          pre-empt lower behaviors)


          - Set to NONE (or SELF only) -


          Directional
          checks (front/behind) unless smoothed


          Random/utility conditions


          Anything
          that flickers a lot'
